From 474f0e5fd8ec1a3574497e1168e3580f0379f26c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ggbdpq <ggbdpq@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 07:30:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gateway: a Chat tool call naming no function is dropped, not
 sent to be refused
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

AricRedemption on #1475: a long Qoder turn ended with an upstream tool
call whose function.name was no string, and the client that checks the
shape of every frame (the AI SDK) refused the whole reply — "Expected
'function.name' to be a string" — the turn not retryable and the call
already in the conversation's history, so the session was dead; the
gateway's own log said status=200, done=true. The parsers that read a
call a model wrote into its text already refuse a nameless one
(textcalls' parser wants a name among the tools offered), but the calls
an upstream made itself went out as they came: chatWholeEvents numbered
a whole reply's calls and patched nothing else, chatTidy's repairs only
dropped an empty repeated name on later fragments, and chatWhole gave
ids and mended the finish, never the name.

A call no client can read runs nowhere, so it is no call: it is dropped
— what the family does with a written block naming no offered tool —
with the later fragments of the same call in a stream, and a finish of
tool_calls with no call left ends stop, as a reply that made no call.
Every path a Chat reply leaves by: a stream relayed as it comes
(chatTidy), a whole reply relayed as one (chatWhole) and a whole reply
given to the agent as the stream it asked for (chatWholeEvents), whose
input need not have been through chatWhole (a reply under a type that
says neither JSON nor a stream). A name the client reads as a string,
empty included, goes as it came: the translations' names are strings by
construction, and a nameless call there fails as an unknown tool — one
tool lost, not the session.

TestNamelessCallStreamDropped, TestNameAbsentStreamDropped,
TestNamelessCallBesideAGoodOne, TestNamelessCallWholeDropped and
TestNamelessCallWholeAsStreamDropped fail on 7dd965ed and pass now;
TestChatCallsEndToolCalls, TestEmptyCallID*, TestTextWritten* and
TestQuietWholeReplyStreamed stand. relayedChat's reader no longer
indexes a name that was never sent. gofmt -l clean.

Fixes #1475
